From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:13:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: rename a group when the Messaging app asks

The app's group rename reaches the plug-in as the transport's
"webos-im-group-rename" signal (account, the group's purple name, the
new name), taken (TRUE) by the plug-in whose account it is.

TDLib's setChatTitle gives the title, for a basic group and a
supergroup alike. The name is sent without the blanks around it; one
longer than Telegram keeps (128 characters, as TDLib 1.8.67's
ChatManager::MAX_TITLE_LENGTH counts them, by Unicode code point) is
cut there, never inside a character, as TDLib's clean_name would cut
it anyway, so that what is sent is what the group gets. A name that is
empty after that, or not UTF-8, is not taken, nor is a chat that is
not a group we are in.

Why a rename failed (no rights) is told in the group, and logged by
the chat's id, without the name. The new title comes back as TDLib's
updateChatTitle, which renames the chat in the buddy list and so the
thread, and as messageChatChangeTitle, our own shown as a notice as
one made elsewhere is.

The cut is webos::groupTitle in webos-send.cpp. Unit tests in
test/webos-commands-test.cpp.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
